# Companion to context_symmetry.bngl: the same defect seen from the SAMPLER
# side rather than the propensity side (RuleMonkey GH #33).
#
# Counting an untransformed reactant pattern once per COMPLEX changes the
# propensity, but a bimolecular rule also has to reject draws that put both
# reactants in the same complex (BNGL's `+` means two distinct complexes).
# That rejection is only self-consistent if the reactant is DRAWN the same way
# it is COUNTED.  Count per complex while still drawing per molecule and the
# rejection rate no longer offsets the propensity, leaving a systematic bias.
#
# The bias cancels exactly whenever every complex holds the same number of
# context matches, which is why no model in the regular corpus can see it.
# This one makes the multiplicities UNEQUAL -- 4 Ez in the tethered complex,
# 1 in the free one -- and puts every Sub inside a complex that also holds Ez,
# so the rejection actually fires and its weighting matters:
#
#   per complex, own complex excluded (correct):  mu = kc*(T+D-1)         = 3*kc
#   per molecule (RuleMonkey before the fix):     mu = kc*(m*(T-1)+D)     = 6*kc
#   per-complex count + per-molecule draw:        mu = kc*(T+D)*(1-m/(m*T+D))
#                                                    = 2.4*kc
#
# with T=2 tethered complexes, D=2 free Ez, m=4 Ez per tethered complex.  The
# three are 25% apart at t_end, so a run that lands on the third is diagnosing
# the sampler and not the count.
#
# Complex instance counts are deliberately tiny (4 complexes), because the bias
# is O(1/#complexes) -- it is a same-complex-pair effect against an O(N^2)
# propensity.  Molecule counts are kept up by chaining several Sub into each
# complex, which is also what keeps the expanded network small enough for BNG2.

begin model
begin parameters
  kc  0.001
  T   2      # tethered complexes: 4 Sub + 4 Ez each
  D   2      # free single-Ez complexes
end parameters

begin molecule types
  Sub(s~0~1,l,r)
  Ez(d,e,f)
end molecule types

begin seed species
  Sub(s~0,l,r!1).Sub(s~0,l!1,r!2).Sub(s~0,l!2,r!3).Sub(s~0,l!3,r!4).Ez(d,e!4,f!5).Ez(d,e!5,f!6).Ez(d,e!6,f!7).Ez(d,e!7,f)  T
  Ez(d,e,f)  D
end seed species

begin observables
  Molecules Sub0  Sub(s~0)
  Molecules Sub1  Sub(s~1)
end observables

begin reaction rules
  R_ctx: Sub(s~0) + Ez(d) -> Sub(s~1) + Ez(d)  kc
end reaction rules
end model

begin actions
  writeXML({overwrite=>1})
end actions
